subproblem.statement:
Let P, m ∈ ℕ and let β : ℝ^P → Λ^{m+1}(ℝ^P) be a continuous (m+1)-form on ℝ^P = Euclid P (β : DifferentialForm (Euclid P) (m + 1), Continuous β). For a continuous (m+1)-form γ and x ∈ ℝ^P put (Kγ)(x) := ∫_0^1 t^m • ι_x(γ(t x)) dt ∈ Λ^m (interval integral over [0, 1] in Covector (Euclid P) m), where ι_xα := α.curryLeft x, i.e. ι_xα(v) = α(Fin.cons x v). Write |α|_E := covectorEuclideanNorm α (Euclidean coefficient norm). Then:
(1) (Kβ)(x)(v) = ∫_0^1 t^m · β(t x)(Fin.cons x v) dt for all x ∈ ℝ^P and v : Fin m → ℝ^P;
(2) for every c ∈ ℝ with |β(y)|_E ≤ c for all y ∈ ℝ^P, |(Kβ)(x)|_E ≤ ‖x‖·c for every x ∈ ℝ^P;
(3) for every x ∈ ℝ^P with β(t x) = 0 for all t ∈ [0, 1], (Kβ)(x) = 0;
(4) for every continuous (m+1)-form β' and every x, K(β + β')(x) = (Kβ)(x) + (Kβ')(x), where β + β' is the pointwise sum;
(5) for every c ∈ ℝ and every x, K(c β)(x) = c • (Kβ)(x), where c β is the pointwise scalar multiple.
